---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Visual parts atlas" description="A visual guide to the major exterior, engine-bay, cabin, brake, and chassis areas of the 2021 Volvo S60 range.">
  <h1>Visual parts atlas</h1>
  <p class="atlas-intro">Choose a view, then select a marked area or a component name to open its reference page. This is a visual navigation guide, not a VIN-specific factory parts catalogue.</p>
  <div class="atlas-key"><span class="atlas-dot"></span> Select a marker or component label to open its reference</div>

  <section class="atlas-section" id="exterior">
    <div class="atlas-heading"><span>01 / Exterior</span><h2>Body and exterior fittings</h2></div>
    <figure class="atlas-figure exterior-view">
      <img src="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/2019_Volvo_S60_T5,_front_1.26.20.jpg?width=1600" alt="Front three-quarter view of a 2019 third-generation Volvo S60" loading="lazy" />
      <a class="atlas-pin" style="--x:76%;--y:57%" href="/exterior/body/" aria-label="Headlamps and front lighting">01</a>
      <a class="atlas-pin" style="--x:68%;--y:68%" href="/exterior/body/" aria-label="Front grille and bumper">02</a>
      <a class="atlas-pin" style="--x:56%;--y:78%" href="/maintenance/tires-wheels/" aria-label="Wheels and tires">03</a>
      <a class="atlas-pin" style="--x:42%;--y:43%" href="/exterior/body/" aria-label="Side mirrors and glass">04</a>
      <a class="atlas-pin" style="--x:33%;--y:70%" href="/exterior/body/" aria-label="Doors and body panels">05</a>
      <figcaption>Representative third-generation S60 exterior. Marker positions are navigational, not factory part callouts.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="atlas-links">
      <a href="/exterior/body/"><b>01</b> Headlamps, tail lamps and exterior lighting</a>
      <a href="/exterior/body/"><b>02</b> Grille, bumpers and trim</a>
      <a href="/maintenance/tires-wheels/"><b>03</b> Wheels, tires and wheel hardware</a>
      <a href="/exterior/body/"><b>04</b> Mirrors, windows and glass</a>
      <a href="/exterior/body/"><b>05</b> Doors, hood, trunk and body panels</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="atlas-section" id="engine-bay">
    <div class="atlas-heading"><span>02 / Engine bay</span><h2>Engine and under-hood systems</h2></div>
    <figure class="atlas-figure engine-view">
      <img src="https://www.volvocars.com/media/support-content/img4b4a330b573d9c4ec0a801524b07b5d5_1_--_--_VOICEpnghigh.png" alt="Volvo 2021 S60 engine compartment with numbered service-point callouts" loading="lazy" />
      <figcaption>Official 2021 S60 owner's-manual illustration. Volvo notes that the layout varies by engine and model variant. Select the engine-compartment overview for component descriptions.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="atlas-links">
      <a href="/technical/engine-compartment/"><b>06</b> Engine oil filler and engine-bay overview</a>
      <a href="/technical/engine-and-drivetrain/"><b>07</b> Turbocharger, supercharger and intake differences</a>
      <a href="/technical/cooling-system/"><b>08</b> Coolant expansion tank and cooling system</a>
      <a href="/technical/fuses/"><b>09</b> Engine-compartment fusebox</a>
      <a href="/maintenance/fluids/"><b>10</b> Fluid specifications and capacities</a>
      <a href="/technical/battery-electrical/"><b>11</b> 12-volt and high-voltage electrical systems</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="atlas-section" id="interior">
    <div class="atlas-heading"><span>03 / Cabin</span><h2>Interior, controls and infotainment</h2></div>
    <figure class="atlas-figure interior-view">
      <img src="https://www.volvocars.com/media/support-content/img028459637a80b16dc0a801526df36585_1_--_--_VOICEpnghigh.png" alt="Volvo Sensus-era cockpit with driver display, steering wheel and center display" loading="lazy" />
      <a class="atlas-pin" style="--x:30%;--y:45%" href="/interior/seats-controls/" aria-label="Steering wheel and driver controls">12</a>
      <a class="atlas-pin" style="--x:54%;--y:31%" href="/infotainment/" aria-label="Infotainment display">13</a>
      <a class="atlas-pin" style="--x:55%;--y:70%" href="/interior/seats-controls/" aria-label="Center console and gear selector">14</a>
      <a class="atlas-pin" style="--x:83%;--y:72%" href="/interior/seats-controls/" aria-label="Seats and cabin trim">15</a>
      <figcaption>Volvo 2021 S60 dashboard and display reference. Inset panels show example driver-display symbols; optional equipment varies by build.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="atlas-links">
      <a href="/interior/seats-controls/"><b>12</b> Steering wheel, stalks and driver controls</a>
      <a href="/infotainment/"><b>13</b> Displays, audio and infotainment</a>
      <a href="/interior/seats-controls/"><b>14</b> Center console, shifter and storage</a>
      <a href="/interior/seats-controls/"><b>15</b> Seats, adjustment and cabin trim</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="atlas-section" id="brakes">
    <div class="atlas-heading"><span>04 / Brakes and chassis</span><h2>Braking, wheels and running gear</h2></div>
    <figure class="atlas-figure brake-view">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 820 330" role="img" aria-labelledby="atlas-brake-title atlas-brake-desc">
        <title id="atlas-brake-title">Disc brake component overview</title>
        <desc id="atlas-brake-desc">Conceptual side cutaway of a disc brake showing rotor, brake pads, caliper, piston and carrier.</desc>
        <rect x="8" y="8" width="804" height="314" rx="14" fill="#f5f8fc" stroke="#d4dfeb"/>
        <circle cx="255" cy="164" r="112" fill="#d9e2eb" stroke="#40566d" stroke-width="7"/>
        <circle cx="255" cy="164" r="35" fill="#f5f8fc" stroke="#40566d" stroke-width="5"/>
        <circle cx="255" cy="164" r="10" fill="#40566d"/>
        <path d="M245 54 H265 V274 H245 Z" fill="#8498ac" stroke="#40566d" stroke-width="3"/>
        <rect x="190" y="88" width="28" height="152" rx="4" fill="#d5a326" stroke="#76570f" stroke-width="3"/>
        <rect x="292" y="88" width="28" height="152" rx="4" fill="#d5a326" stroke="#76570f" stroke-width="3"/>
        <path d="M165 70 H345 Q382 70 382 108 V220 Q382 258 345 258 H320" fill="none" stroke="#17639d" stroke-width="17" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        <path d="M365 80 V250" stroke="#52677d" stroke-width="10"/>
        <g stroke="#52677d" stroke-width="2" fill="none">
          <path d="M255 52 V28 H450"/><path d="M202 88 L130 54 H40"/><path d="M382 115 L475 80 H580"/><path d="M365 250 L475 280 H580"/>
        </g>
        <g fill="#173b5d" font-size="16" font-weight="700">
          <text x="460" y="33">Rotor / disc</text>
          <text x="42" y="48">Brake pad</text>
          <text x="590" y="84">Caliper body</text>
          <text x="590" y="286">Carrier / bracket</text>
        </g>
        <text x="410" y="310" text-anchor="middle" fill="#64788d" font-size="12">Conceptual component illustration — not an S60 parts drawing</text>
      </svg>
      <figcaption>Conceptual brake component map; exact 2021 S60 hardware varies by axle and brake package. Open the brake assembly guide for component functions and VIN-fitment cautions.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="atlas-links">
      <a href="/repairs/brake-assembly/"><b>16</b> Brake discs / rotors</a>
      <a href="/repairs/front-brake-pads/"><b>17</b> Pads, calipers and pad hardware</a>
      <a href="/maintenance/tires-wheels/"><b>18</b> Hubs, wheels and tire fitment</a>
      <a href="/technical/awd-system/"><b>19</b> AWD, propeller shaft and rear drive</a>
      <a href="/technical/suspension-steering/"><b>20</b> Suspension, steering and chassis</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="note"><strong>Identification note.</strong> The photographs are representative visual references, not images of every component on this exact car. The numbered markers are navigation links, not OEM callout numbers. Use the VIN-specific Volvo parts catalogue to confirm part numbers, variants and fitment.</div>

  <h2>Image credits</h2>
  <ul class="atlas-credits">
    <li>Exterior: Kevauto, <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2019_Volvo_S60_T5,_front_1.26.20.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">2019 Volvo S60 T5, front</a>, CC BY-SA 4.0.</li>
    <li>Engine bay: Volvo Cars, <a href="https://www.volvocars.com/uk/support/car/s60/2021/article/f3e117dc70239324c0a801513d2de23c/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">2021 S60 engine compartment overview</a>.</li>
    <li>Interior/display: Volvo Cars, <a href="https://www.volvocars.com/uk/support/car/s60/2020/article/f6848b197ef39a36c0a80151207886f7/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Sensus — online connectivity and entertainment</a>.</li>
    <li>Brake component drawing: original conceptual SVG created for this reference; not an OEM Volvo parts illustration.</li>
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>
